CREATE TABLE info(
    id INT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    age INT CHECK (age >= 18 AND age<=99),
    phone VARCHAR(15) DEFAULT 'N/A'
)

NOT NULL   → value must exist (value cannot be NULL)
UNIQUE     → duplicate values not allowed
PRIMARY KEY → uniquely identifies row -> UNIQUE + NOT NULL

FOREIGN KEY → maintains relationship -> references primary key of another table
CHECK      → value must satisfy a condition
DEFAULT    → automatically provides a value


composite primary key -> mix of primary keys for ex mix of stud-Id and course_id but both must be unique 
